<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>7.15.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02016</md:content-id>
    <md:title>7.15.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>a9c82f0e-6ad5-44bc-90e2-3c0a5bf6e8ce</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section class="practice" id="sect-00001"><para id="para-00001">Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<section id="sect-00002"><exercise id="c133d14f-dfe1-4d87-983d-a394d9d888d3" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00001"><para id="para-00002"><emphasis>Select three</emphasis> quadratic expressions written in vertex form.</para>
      </problem><solution id="sol-00001"><para id="para-00003">Correct! <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00004">Try again. Revisit activities 7.14.2 – 7.14.3.</para><para id="para-00005">The correct answers are: <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="_7b0b1508-7cef-415d-80fd-59c5381859fa" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00002"><para id="para-00006">Examine the following two equations and use them to answer questions 2 – 5. One defines function <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>m</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> and the other defines function <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>p</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.</para><para id="para-00007"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>m</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00008"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>p</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>9</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00009">How do you know that the expressions defining <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>m</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>p</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> are equivalent?</para>
      <para id="para-00010">Multiple Choice:</para><para id="para-00011">Both expressions are equal to <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.</para><para id="para-00012">Both expressions are equal to <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.</para><para id="para-00013">Both expressions are equal to <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para><para id="para-00014">Both expressions are equal to <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para></problem><solution id="sol-00002"><para id="para-00015">Correct! Both expressions are equal to <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>. <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>9</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>9</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>9</m:mn><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>9</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.</para><para id="para-00016">Try again. Revisit activities 7.14.2 and 7.14.3.</para><para id="para-00017">The correct answer is: Both expressions are equal to <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>. <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>9</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>9</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>9</m:mn><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>9</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="db7fd02c-7b6a-46cf-b8e0-55761c276bb8" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00003"><para id="para-00018">Recall <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>m</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>p</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>9</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>. What is the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate of the vertex of the graph of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>m</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
      </problem><solution id="sol-00003"><para id="para-00019">Correct! The <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate of the vertex of this function is -3.</para><para id="para-00020">Try again. Revisit activity 7.14.4.</para><para id="para-00021">The correct answer is -3. The <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate of the vertex of this function is -3.</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="c98bb928-4560-4c4b-bbf4-ea0149ca6437" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00004"><para id="para-00022">Recall <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>m</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>p</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>9</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>. What is the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate of the vertex of the graph of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>m</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
      </problem><solution id="sol-00004"><para id="para-00023">Correct! The <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate of the vertex of this function is -9.</para><para id="para-00024">Try again. Revisit activity 7.14.4.</para><para id="para-00025">The correct answer is -9. The <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate of the vertex of this function is -9.</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="_32b1b9fd-9c8e-42a7-819e-b7a0dd0c09da" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00005"><para id="para-00026">Recall <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>m</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>p</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>9</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>. What are the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercepts of the graph of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>p</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
      <para id="para-00027">Multiple Choice:</para><para id="para-00028"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00029"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00030"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00031"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para></problem><solution id="sol-00005"><para id="para-00032">Correct! (0,0) and (-6,0) The graphs of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>m</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>p</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> are the same. The zeros of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>m</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> are 0 and -6, which give the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercepts of the graph.</para><para id="para-00033">Try again. Revisit activity 7.15.3.</para><para id="para-00034">The correct answer is:(0,0) and (-6,0). The graphs of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>m</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>p</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> are the same. The zeros of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>m</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> are 0 and -6, which give the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercepts of the graph.</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="_74d02381-b4db-4a6f-905a-364096b5a335" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00006"><para id="para-00035">For questions 6 – 11, enter the coordinates of the vertex of the graph that represents the equation.</para><para id="para-00036">Find the coordinates of the vertex for the equation <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
      <para id="para-00037">What is the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate of the vertex?</para>
      
    </problem><solution id="sol-00006"><para id="para-00038">Correct! The <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate of the vertex of this function is 3.</para><para id="para-00039">Try again. Revisit activity 7.15.4.</para><para id="para-00040">The correct answer is 3. The <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate of the vertex of this function is 3.</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="_8db0a037-729b-45cc-99dd-29ba0eb6651d" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00007"><para id="para-00041">What is the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate of the vertex?</para>
      </problem><solution id="sol-00007"><para id="para-00042">Correct! The <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate of the vertex of this function is 5.</para><para id="para-00043">Try again. Revisit activity 7.15.4.</para><para id="para-00044">The correct answer is 5. The <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate of the vertex of this function is 5.</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="_531c5ab7-b573-41b0-a0e6-72810f62ea29" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00008"><para id="para-00045">Find the coordinates of the vertex for the equation <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
      <para id="para-00046">What is the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate of the vertex?</para>
      </problem><solution id="sol-00008"><para id="para-00047">Correct! The <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate of the vertex of this function is -7.</para><para id="para-00048">Try again. Revisit activity 7.15.4.</para><para id="para-00049">The correct answer is -7. The <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate of the vertex of this function is -7.</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="_835917d0-a687-4630-ab31-da7b539992df" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00009"><para id="para-00050">What is the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate of the vertex?</para>
      </problem><solution id="sol-00009"><para id="para-00051">Correct! The <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate of the vertex of this function is 3.</para><para id="para-00052">Try again. Revisit activity 7.15.4.</para><para id="para-00053">The correct answer is 3. The <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate of the vertex of this function is 3.</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="_50d774b8-4213-4075-b64d-5439c4ae7b4e" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00010"><para id="para-00054">Find the coordinates of the vertex for the equation <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
      <para id="para-00055">What is the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate of the vertex?</para>
      </problem><solution id="sol-00010"><para id="para-00056">Correct! The <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate of the vertex of this function is 4.</para><para id="para-00057">Try again. Revisit activity 7.15.4.</para><para id="para-00058">The correct answer is 4. The <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate of the vertex of this function is 4.</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="b848525e-136a-4158-9b48-dea628bbb367" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00011"><para id="para-00059">What is the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate of the vertex?</para>
