      <exercise id="_153bf41c-176e-4750-8244-eb98aa10b803" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00018"><para id="para-00090">For questions 12 – 14, answer the questions about the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>- and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinates of the vertex, and whether the function opens up or down.</para><para id="para-00091">For function <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, find the coordinates of the vertex and determine if the function opens up or down.</para>
